!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/link/valid/a-value-entry-reaches-a-key-through-a-spaced-field-name-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/link-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.12, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-DATA] §2.4 (reference reach, proposed for Revision 40)"
  description: """
    Each segment of a reference is a name of the family of what it enters. `main` is a value of `site`, whose
    `name_type` is `word`, so `public api` is a name of that family and selects the field so named; the field holds
    an `api`, keyed by `meta.identifier`, so `ping` selects its key. A segment holding a space is written by quoting
    the whole name, one token split at `.`.
    """
  valid: {
    binds: [h main]
  }
}
